S-RED finding: MkBayesianServer — Reconnect after OS-killed process hangs forever

## Symptom

If the detached MCMC process is killed by the OS (OOM killer, SIGKILL,
system shutdown) without writing any signal file (mkp_done.signal,
mkp_error.txt, or mkp_cancel.signal), then:

1. User reopens the app and clicks "Reconnect".
2. No signal files are found → `rv$status <- "running"`.
3. The poll observer fires every 5 s indefinitely.
4. `rv$proc` is NULL (lost after session restart) so no liveness check
   is possible via `proc$is_alive()`.
5. There is no timeout and no way for the app to auto-detect the dead
   process — the UI is stuck in "Running…" forever.

## Proposed fix

On Reconnect, when no signal files are present, check whether the stored
PID is still alive before defaulting to "running":

```r
pidAlive <- .PidIsAlive(job$pid)
if (!pidAlive) {
  rv$status <- "error"
  rv$errorMsg <- sprintf(
    "Process PID %d is no longer running and left no completion signal.\n
     The run may have been killed by the OS (OOM, shutdown). Partial log
     data (if any) is still available in %s.", job$pid, job$logDir)
  shiny::showNotification(rv$errorMsg, type = "error", duration = 20)
  return()
}
```

Where `.PidIsAlive(pid)` uses the `ps` package if available, otherwise
falls back to a platform-appropriate check:

```r
.PidIsAlive <- function(pid) {
  if (is.na(pid) || pid <= 0L) return(FALSE)
  if (requireNamespace("ps", quietly = TRUE)) {
    h <- tryCatch(ps::ps_handle(pid = pid), error = function(e) NULL)
    return(!is.null(h) && tryCatch(ps::ps_is_running(h), error = function(e) FALSE))
  }
  # Fallback: platform-specific
  if (.Platform$OS.type == "windows") {
    out <- system2("tasklist", c("/FI", paste0("PID eq ", pid), "/NH"),
                   stdout = TRUE, stderr = FALSE)
    return(any(grepl(as.character(pid), out, fixed = TRUE)))
  }
  # POSIX: signal 0 tests existence without killing
  tryCatch(tools::pskill(pid, 0L) == 0L, error = function(e) FALSE)
}
```

Add `ps` to Suggests if this is implemented.

## Found by

Agent E, S-RED pass on M-078/M-079 (2026-03-27).
